# DTF tier manifest: conda-allowlist-hosted-members
#   (artifact-keeper#5055; fixed in 1.11.9 and 1.12.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=mock-conda (the conda-channel-types
# tier's stdlib-python static conda channel on 172.16.<slot>.70; it publishes
# dtfup-alpha 1.0 and 2.0 and dtfup-blocked 1.0 in noarch) + client=conda (a
# real micromamba 2.0 client on the DTF network).
#
# THE BUG
# #5055  The package allowlist of a virtual conda channel (#4576) filtered only
#        what REMOTE members contributed. Hosted (local/staging) members passed
#        through unfiltered in every index form and on downloads, so the
#        channel served packages outside its list: anyone who could publish to
#        a hosted member put a package on every channel containing it. Fixed:
#        the list applies to every member by default, in repodata.json (plain,
#        .zst, .bz2), current_repodata.json, channeldata.json, the CEP-16 shard
#        index (main) and on downloads through the virtual; a hosted package
#        the list does not admit is dropped and still owns its name (the
#        upstream's records of that name stay out). A per-channel opt-out,
#        `"scope": "remote_only"`, restores pass-through. Direct reads of the
#        hosted repository are unchanged.
#
# RED image: ak-backend:1.11.8 (every FIX case). GREEN: 1.11.9 and 1.12.0.
#
# The shard index and its shards, run_exports.json and the CEP-50 `.sigs` /
# `.sigs.<sha256>` sidecars are asserted too (RED on sha-b2d0bcc, the parent of
# the fix on main): the unlisted hosted package and its owned name are not in
# the virtual's shard index and their shards are 404 by address through it,
# run_exports.json leaves them out, and the hidden package's sidecars are 404
# through the virtual, while the listed package keeps its shard, run_exports
# record and sidecar, and the hosted repository serves everything directly.
# For the sidecars the oracle recreates the backend once at the start with a
# P-256 key it generates (fixtures/attestation-key.yml,
# CONDA_ATTESTATION_PUBLIC_KEYS) and attests both hosted packages with it.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one admin login then ~40 authenticated calls back
# to back. UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the remote's upstream is the mock
# on a private address (the profile also scopes AK_SSRF_ALLOW_PRIVATE_CIDRS).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-conda client.conda"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
COVERS="5055"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
